.TH ZERODDS-AMQP-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-amqp-bridged \- DDS to AMQP 1.0 bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-amqp-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-broker\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS=ADDR\fR]...
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-amqp-bridged
is a client of an AMQP 1.0 broker on one side and a DDS participant on the
other. Each topic of the configuration has a sender link (DDS samples to the
broker), a receiver link (broker messages into DDS) or both, on a session of
its own. SASL PLAIN, SCRAM-SHA-256, SCRAM-SHA-512, EXTERNAL, ANONYMOUS and XOAUTH2; TLS with
ALPN
.IR amqp ;
the sender and receiver settle modes of the topic; a topic catalog per
connection; reconnect with back-off. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-amqp-bridge-daemon-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
YAML config (Spec \(sc3). See
.BR zerodds-amqp-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-broker =\fIURL\fR
AMQP broker URL
.RI ( amqp:// ", " amqps:// ).
.TP
.BR \-\-container\-id =\fIID\fR
AMQP container-id; it also seeds the GUID prefix of the DDS participant.
Default
.IR zerodds\-bridge\-<host> :
the host name with its dots as hyphens, at most 32 characters.
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID.
.TP
.BR \-\-sasl\-mechanism =\fINAME\fR
One of
.IR PLAIN ", " SCRAM\-SHA\-256 ", " SCRAM\-SHA\-512 ", " EXTERNAL ", " ANONYMOUS ", " XOAUTH2 .
.TP
.BR \-\-user =\fIUSER\fR
SASL username.
.TP
.BR \-\-password =\fIPASS\fR
SASL password.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-ca =\fIFILE\fR
TLS CA certificate.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS client cert.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS client key.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS=ADDR\fR
One topic mapping, repeatable: an entry of
.B topics
with the DDS topic name and the AMQP address, both directions; the short
form of
.BR "\-\-set +topics=" \fIDDS=ADDR\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error :
the threshold of the log, one JSON object per line on stdout with
.BR timestamp ", " level ", " event ", " container_id
and the fields of the event;
.I debug
adds a line per transfer
.RB ( transfer_in ", " transfer_out ", " disposition )
with
.BR delivery_id ", " bytes " and " latency_us .
Only the error that ends the program goes to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.PP
Test hooks. Real options, documented because the program accepts them
and an option nobody can find is one nobody maintains.
.TP
.BR \-\-once
Serve one connection, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-connect\-timeout\-ms =\fIN\fR
Give up connecting after \fIN\fR milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle. The values of
.B amqp.sasl.password
and
.B amqp.cbs.secret
are shown as ***, also in the origin of a
.BR \-\-set .
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon: it takes no further DDS samples, waits
up to 30 s for the broker to settle the deliveries in flight, then detaches
every link, ends every session, closes the connection and exits with 0.
The log line
.B drain_started
marks the start of this drain. What is left (unsettled deliveries,
messages waiting for credit) is counted and logged. On Windows CTRL_C and CTRL_BREAK stop the daemon the
same way. Closing the console, logoff and system shutdown end the process
without this drain: Windows ends it as soon as the console control handler
returns.
SIGHUP reads the configuration again: a right withdrawn from the topic ACL
applies at once, the TLS material to the next connect; a newly granted
right, changed topics, broker address or domain need a restart and are
logged. A configuration that does not load changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP/HTTP collector, such as http://localhost:4318: every TRANSFER
round trip is a trace
.B amqp.transfer
with the child
.B dds.write
(AMQP to DDS) or
.B dds.read
(DDS to AMQP), sent every 5 seconds and when the program ends.
.TP
.B AMQP_PASSWORD
The SASL password; the setting
.BR amqp.sasl.password .
The environment is the lowest layer above the built-in defaults: a password
in a configuration file,
.B \-\-password
and
.B \-\-set
win over it.
.TP
.B AMQP_CBS_SECRET
The shared access key of claims-based security; the setting
.BR amqp.cbs.secret ,
beneath the files, as
.BR AMQP_PASSWORD .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown, or
.B \-\-check\-config
found the configuration valid.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid configuration: a value, the broker URL, the SASL settings, the TLS
files.
.TP
.B 2
With
.BR \-\-once ,
the TCP connect failed or the broker connection was lost (without it a TCP
failure is retried after the back-off); with
.BR \-\-check\-config ,
a configuration file could not be read or does not parse.
.TP
.B 3
The DDS participant or one of its endpoints could not be created.
.TP
.B 4
The TLS handshake failed (certificate, protocol, ALPN, the connection reset)
before the first connection stood.
.TP
.B 5
The SASL exchange failed (mechanism not offered, authentication refused)
before the first connection stood.
.TP
.B 6
The broker refused the open (it answered with a close or reset the
connection) before the first connection stood, or its open does not fit the bridge (fewer channels than
links). A time-out in these stages, and every failure after a connection
stood, is retried after the back-off.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/amqp-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-amqp-bridged.yaml (5).
